From: pocknix
Subject: [PATCH] battery: prefer current_now x voltage_now on Snapdragon pmic-glink

REBASED for MangoHud e1430aba (the Valve/Deckard base, v0.8.4-184-ge1430aba).
Originally 0004-Qualcomm-battery-power-now.patch, written against v0.8.4.

WHY: Snapdragon pmic-glink firmware (AYN Odin 3 / Thor) reports power_now an
order of magnitude off while current_now/voltage_now are correct. Prefer the
current x voltage pair and keep power_now only as a fallback, read as 10 uW
units to undo the reported 10x error. This is the same behaviour our decky
battery reader already implements (packages/pocknix-decky/
panel-de-control/py_modules/battery/reader.py). Upstream still prefers
power_now (div 1e6); NOT upstream.

STATUS: needs validation on the Odin (A/B wattage with the overlay).
---
diff --git a/src/battery.cpp b/src/battery.cpp
index e87b2a6..a433618 100644
--- a/src/battery.cpp
+++ b/src/battery.cpp
@@ -161,16 +161,10 @@ float BatteryStats::getPower() {
         if (deckard)
             continue;
 
-        // Prefer power_now (µW) when available.
-        if (fs::exists(power_now)) {
-            std::ifstream input(power_now);
-            std::string line;
-            if (std::getline(input, line)) {
-                power_w += std::fabs(stof(line)) / 1000000.0f;
-            }
-            continue;
-        }
-
+        // Prefer current_now × voltage_now. Some Snapdragon pmic-glink firmwares
+        // (AYN handhelds) report power_now an order of magnitude off while the
+        // current/voltage pair is right, so power_now is only a fallback (read as
+        // 10 µW units to undo the reported 10× error).
         if (fs::exists(current_now) && fs::exists(voltage_now)) {
             float i_ua = 0.0f;
             float v_uv = 0.0f;
@@ -192,6 +186,15 @@ float BatteryStats::getPower() {
 
             power_w += (std::fabs(i_ua) * std::fabs(v_uv)) * 1e-12f;
         }
+
+        else if (fs::exists(power_now)) {
+            std::ifstream input(power_now);
+            std::string line;
+            if (std::getline(input, line)) {
+                power_w += std::fabs(stof(line)) / 10000000.0f;
+            }
+            continue;
+        }
     }
 
     // Keep previous power on empty or invalid reads
